  "description": "Renders author-created HTML pages with CSS styling into PDF documents via the CodeBrix.PdfDocCreate document object model. Applies a documented subset of CSS - inline style attributes, style blocks, and linked local stylesheets - with real selector matching, cascade, specificity, and inheritance. Embeds every image format CodeBrix.Imaging decodes plus SVG (referenced files, data: URIs, and inline svg elements, rasterized identically on Windows, macOS, and Linux). All text is rendered with the CodeBrix.Platform.Fonts Roboto (sans-serif), Merriweather (serif), and Roboto Mono (monospace) font packages - plus any fonts the consumer registers - so output is identical on every operating system. Designed for HTML/CSS written for PDF generation, not for repurposing arbitrary web pages.",
  "iconFile": "icon-codebrix-128.png",
